From cf173f2e995c8d4c2ee7e4ec528f950c37d239fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:52:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Cantilever Case 7: root plate runs on under the face trusses;
 trusses meet the base exactly

A wide chord (the root plate) ending where only narrower members carry on runs on
as far as the TO does near both its edges (x = 55.5, was 43.2: the skeleton stops
half a width short). The face trusses' side on a layer, and their chords there,
are set at the layer's depth exactly (the rounded outline left a 4e-4 mm gap and
three solids).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BdLZZ8R4FqXDzDRWDvVnZQ
